# sweep: --seed-root examples/books/fixtures/chapters
# A copy of what was kept in The Lock Keeper's Year. With nothing kept the
# notes offer no copy. After a paragraph is marked and a page bookmarked they
# do: the copy is saved on the reader, says when it is ready, and the paired
# computer receives it as a Markdown file.
wait-for Lock Keeper
tap The Lock Keeper
wait-for Spring
tap-id reader-controls
wait-for Page 1 of
tap-id reader-highlights
wait-for Nothing is marked in this book yet.
expect-missing Save a copy
tap Mark a paragraph
wait-for Tap a paragraph to mark it
tap-id reader-mark-2
wait-for Marked:
tap Back to the book
wait-idle
tap-id reader-controls
tap-id reader-bookmark
wait-for Bookmarked
tap-id reader-highlights
wait-for Marked passages
expect Bookmarks
expect Save a copy
shot books-copy-notes
tap Save a copy
wait-for Ready for your computer.
expect The Lock Keeper's Year notes
shot books-copy-ready
companion export --app books --sim --out target/sim-check/books-notes
# Back from the copy returns to the notes it was asked for from.
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for Marked passages
expect Save a copy
tap Back to the book
wait-for Spring
